  87: 
  88: The ARF-Net shows a statistically significant improvement in AUC, shifted away from the baseline's CI.
  89: 
  90: \subsection{Ablation Study}
  91: Ablation across feature subsets (Kinematics, Risk, ARF Full) shows that while kinematics drive the primary detection, the Hessian eigenvalues are required for directional explainability (EGRT) without sacrificing accuracy.
  92: 
  93: \section{Conclusion}
  94: This paper presented an explainable direction-aware safety framework using Anisotropic Risk Fields. By incorporating Hessian-based curvature features, we achieved both statistically significant performance gains on real-world geometry and human-readable reasoning traces.
